{
	title: 'Agent rebase plans and atomic continuation',
	spec: 'User and model commands support /rebase show, preview, run and optional run shorthand. Sparse plans keep unmentioned entries; drop accepts toggle-like IDs/lists/closed and open-ended ranges, bare ranges include all entry kinds, kind prefixes filter. edit takes one entry and a quoted full replacement, with double, single or backtick delimiters and backslash, active delimiter, n and t escapes; reject unsupported escapes, no interpolation or Unicode escapes. Semicolons separate operations. All targets use the shown snapshot, ordinary append-only activity is allowed but intervening context rewrites invalidate it. Open tails resolve through application time, including the executing rebase call/result. Preserve linked call/result/signature/inbox grouping and the append-only audit trail. Apply synchronously between rounds like compact/clear, serialized with normal steering/advisory/queued inbox actions. Failures remain complete and reach the model; failed application drops nothing. Preview uses the same validation/report without mutation and explains open-tail semantics. Successful rebase automatically continues when projected conversation ends with a user prompt, including user/editor initiated rebases; --paused suppresses continuation and ends a model turn. Otherwise a rebase continues only when the last remaining message is one where action continues; an assistant message that ended its turn (followed by its completed turn_end) never continues, whether the user or the model ran the rebase. Continuing model rebases run on rewritten context with actual outcome; self-removed calls/results are not replayed. No arbitrary insertion. Reuse existing plan validation/reporting and keep extra modules lazy. Agent access requires explicit user consent guidance. Invariant: model self-rebase never creates orphan tool results or races incoming messages.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'common/rebase-sparse.ts parses sparse drop/edit operations without evaluation: three quote delimiters, only backslash/active-quote/n/t escapes, literal interpolation syntax, kind-filtered IDs/lists/ranges and application-time open tails. Rows distinguish tool calls from slash-command records even when the tool is named command. The host keeps one shown snapshot per open session using weak metadata keys; ordinary appends are accepted, but rebase/reset/compact/replacement prompts invalidate it. Explicit run or shorthand without show uses the current snapshot.',
		'host/rebase-agent.ts loads lazily and extends the existing durable context-transition output intent with a resolved sparse plan, open tails, originating call, pause and resume flags. The turn loop reserves and preflights the settled result record, writes the actual report or full tool error, then applies synchronously before another inbox/provider boundary. Existing rebase grouping protects calls/results, signed rounds and inbox revisions. A self-removed exchange is not reinserted or converted to a report notice. Recovery recognizes the rebase intent on its commit and writes continuation before completing the intent, so accepted changes apply once across crash gaps.',
		'Sparse user and model rebases continue active turns or trailing prompts; editor/view application also continues trailing prompts unless --paused. Both clients forward the paused flag through rebase-apply, validated as boolean. Editor todo queue lines conflict with --paused and are rejected before mutation with instructions to remove the lines or flag; this preserves the explicit pause instead of silently starting a queued prompt. Undo retains its existing settled-session path; --paused with undo is rejected explicitly rather than ignored.',
		'Content-atomic failure invariant: report generation and expanded-group validation happen before commit. The low-level idle path writes its required pause marker before the rebase record, so a failed rewrite commit drops and edits nothing; its full error states that the original content remains and the session is paused. During an active turn, keep the live status cache until turn settlement so --paused emits the actual paused state. Tests cover quotes/escapes, append versus rewrite staleness, self-removal without replay, retained outcomes, user/editor continuation, paused mode, concurrent steering/advisory/queued delivery, crash recovery, and failed rewrite commits.',
		'Agent help says: Use --paused if user asks. Real use showed an agent adding --paused to a retry request without a user request to pause.',
		'Surviving rebase reports must preserve explicit --paused, dropped ranges/counts and edited entry IDs in the compact first line, including when a model rebase removes its own command. Full diffs remain in expandable detail. This restores visibility of the operation independent of retained command history.',
		'Automatic continuation includes unfinished assistant turns, not only trailing prompts. A retained completion marker belongs to the original final assistant entry: dropping that reply must not mark earlier exposed commentary completed. Reports describe the actual planned continuation as after user prompt or unfinished turn; explicit --paused suppresses both.',
		'Invariant restored: a model rebase run inside its own turn that leaves a turn-ending assistant message last ends the turn as completed instead of requesting again. continuation() checked for a running turn before the completed turn_end, and the turn loop always requested after a rebase; apply()/results() now return done and turns.ts ends the turn.'
